So, a level 11 human wizard with an "oR, speed boots, magic lamp, +4
GoP and the +5 Magicbane walks into a shop. She has identified most
crap but is missing the ?oDA and ?oEA and didn't manage to write one
thanks to icky luck and Mines End lacking a luckstone (!). She buys a
scroll that is particularly suspicious due to its high cost (300
zorkmids, low charisma) and leaves to a monster-free room, takes off
all armor except for a mummy wrapping and begins to read the scroll...
(after taking off +4 GoP she is also burdened with AC 10... -fail-)

"What specie do you want to genocide?" Holy crap... she was all like
'I have a feeling this scroll is cursed... I'm gonna reverse genocide
wraiths so I can gain a few levels...' But then, what if it wasn't
cursed and I ended genociding wraiths? Hmmm... Master mind flayers
then? But the player had made a new sprites for the master mind
flayers and really wanted to see how it looked in action, so she ended
up choosing arch-liches.

Next thing, Fenrir the Magician was against the wall, surrounded by
five arch liches, burdened with AC 10 and magicbane not wielded
(fortunately, she was cold resistant, though!). She teleported to the
staircase, two arch liches following close behind. After engraving the
E word in the upstairs, she managed to escape, but some of the nasties
followed her. She teleported to the stairs again and managed to run
away from the Air elemental; there she re-equips all stuff and
dispatches all the &s and Ts and the air elemental and bravely goes to
face the five arch liches...

They summon nasties, all five of them, and in no time the entire floor
is filled with high level monsters Fenrir stands no chance against.
Master mind flayers (the sprite looked good, by the way),
disenchanters, purple worms, elvenkings, minotaurs, olg hai,
jabberwocks, xorns, iron golems, and.... black dragons!  Fen knew the
deintegration-breathing lizards were her ticket outta there, and so,
looting the bag of holding, she puts on her trusty ring of conflict
along with a =oSD.

Somehow she survives the mind-numbingly annoying "the foo hits the
foo!" messages, gets the dragon to deintegrate three liches and kills
the minotaurs with the help of a /oS. The iron golem digs a hole
through the floor and many nasties fall down, possibly including one
of the liches, the other being destroyed by Magicbane. And so the
level is cleared, the Magician only gaining one level and black dragon
scales. Hm...


